---
source: tests/cli_init.rs
expression: r.stdout
---
init: register `caelestia` by reference
root:     <HOME>/rice/caelestia
profile:  <HOME>/.local/share/ricepilot/profiles/caelestia
baseline: <HOME>/.local/state/ricepilot/baseline/caelestia

by reference means the profile's payload is your own tree. ricepilot reads it,
never writes to it, and never runs an installer over it.

the tree:
  5 director(ies), 5 file(s), 1 symlink(s), 37 byte(s)

  1 absolute symlink(s) inside the tree. ricepilot copies a link as a link and
  never rewrites one, so each of these keeps pointing where it points now:
    zen/userChrome.link -> <HOME>/rice/caelestia/zen/userChrome.css  (back into this tree)

  1 file(s) only their owner can read. a mode-600 file in a config tree is
  usually a token or a key; consider declaring it `volatile` so its content is
  not hashed into a manifest:
    0600  .secret

links in <HOME>/.config that already point into it:
  <HOME>/.config/btop -> <HOME>/rice/caelestia/btop
      not offered: does not point at a directory right now. v1 activates directory links only, and a link into the rice that resolves to nothing is worth looking at before it is registered as healthy
  <HOME>/.config/foot -> <HOME>/rice/caelestia/foot
      would ask whether to adopt this link (it is not moved, retargeted or re-created —
      only recorded as one ricepilot owns, so `switch` can act on it)
  <HOME>/.config/hypr -> <HOME>/rice/caelestia/hypr
      would ask whether to adopt this link (it is not moved, retargeted or re-created —
      only recorded as one ricepilot owns, so `switch` can act on it)
  <HOME>/.config/uwsm -> <HOME>/rice/caelestia/uwsm
      not offered: inside `~/.config/uwsm`, which v1 will not manage under any circumstances

1 owner-only file(s) will be proposed as `volatile`, so their contents are not
hashed into a manifest. they are listed above; it is one question, and the
manifest is yours to edit afterwards.

nothing in <HOME>/.config is moved, created or retargeted by this command. the baseline
is a copy, never a move: your tree stays exactly where it is.

nothing has been changed. re-run with --commit to register it.
--commit asks about each link separately; anything you do not say yes to is left
unregistered, and nothing on the live machine moves either way.
